        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Acorn KS1JI, Stainless Steel Arched Mortise Lockset</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThis forged stainless steel handleset gives off a distinct southwestern feel that makes it perfect for traditional homes. It will grant a rustic touch that isn't too old world but still has historical notes. Each of the indents left by the hammer falls of the blacksmith that made the Stainless Steel Arched Mortise Entryset tells the story of the beautiful textures of the metal from which it was made and the artist who shaped it. The natural stainless steel finish is similar to antique nickel or pewter. It is available in single cylinder and dummy functions. This ball knob mortise lockset is for 1-3/4\" thick doors with a 2-3/4\" backset.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/ACO-Mortise-Specifications.gif?v=1704354518\" width=\"255\" height=\"273\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Acorn Mortise Lock Specifications\">\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nAlso Available Matching: <a href=\"/products/stainless-steel-lined-ball-knobset-acorn-ku5jd\"><b>Stainless Steel Lined Ball Knobset</b></a>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Stainless Steel Arched Mortise Entryset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Finish: <b>Stainless Steel</b></li>\r\n<li>Height: 9-7/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Width: 2-3/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Projection: 2-7/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Knob Diameter: 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset: 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Stile Width: Recommend 4-1/2” with a 4-1/4” minimum.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Dummy Handleset:</b> Blank trim for non-working doors that does not have a turnpiece or a cylinder. It does not latch and does not lock. Usually used as matching trim for the non-working side of double doors.</li>\r\n<li><b>Single Cylinder Handleset:</b> A key operates the deadbolt from the exterior while a thumbturn operates it from the interior. The latch is operated by a knob from both the exterior and the interior.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe handing actually refers to the mortise lock, rather than the knob. <a href=\"/pages/how-to-order-door-hardware\"><b>Click Here to Determine Handing</b></a>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<i>Due to the handmade craftsman nature of this product, all dimensions are approximate. DO NOT DRILL ANY HOLES until you have the actual pieces to be mounted.</i>\r\n</p>",
